    "updated_at": "2022-09-17T19:40:02Z",
    "body": "It seems like both the union conversion & overload resolution algorithms would already behave sensibly if a dot were added to that grid as both have `if IsCallable(V) and there’s a...` branches before dictionary.\r\n\r\nI thought maybe [[LegacyTreatNonObjectAsNull]](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#LegacyTreatNonObjectAsNull) might have been a factor, but it only does its weird thing when nullable and that would preclude it from being in a union with a dictionary in the cases where it needs to be regardless. I’m less certain if that’s also true for overload distinguishability already.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
